<title>ESTONIA: RADIO NOON HEADLINES - MAY 6.</title>
<headline>RADIO NOON HEADLINES - MAY 6.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>These were the main headlines reported by Kuku Radio on Tuesday at noon. Reuters has not verified these reports and cannot vouch for their accuracy.</p>
<p>- Serious staff changes are expected in the interior ministry and police department, daily newspaper Postimees said.</p>
<p>- French President Jacques Chirac said Poland might join the European Union by 2000.</p>
<p>- The management style of Estonian managers is not always adequate, research showed.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
